.TH SUPIVPN-SETUP 8 "October 2026" "SupiVPN" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
supivpn-setup \- configure a combined SupiVPN Debian host
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B supivpn-setup
.I plan|init|check|certificates
.RB [ --config
.IR file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Explicit first-time setup on Debian 13 with systemd. Install matching SupiVPN
packages and PostgreSQL 18 first (postgresql-client-18 for a remote database).
Supply trusted IdP metadata and a valid
server certificate. The example is in
.IR /usr/share/supivpn/examples/setup.example.json .
.PP
The plan action prints intended changes without changing the host.
The init action requires root, refuses existing SupiVPN configuration or state,
generates configuration, keys, restricted database roles and random credentials,
creates the dedicated PostgreSQL 18/supivpn cluster on loopback port 55433,
and runs the installed migrations. It starts only that database cluster.
It does not alter existing clusters, install packages, apply firewall rules,
enable services or start the VPN.
.PP
With the optional database object, init instead uses a pre-provisioned empty
remote PostgreSQL 18 writer. It verifies TLS and restricted login roles before
writing configuration, copies the public CA, saves separate runtime/migration
credentials and applies migrations. It does not create, start, enable or check
a local database cluster. It never transfers an existing database.
.PP
The check action verifies service state and HTTPS readiness using certificate
validation. It does not establish a client tunnel or test the real IdP.
The certificates action validates and refreshes certificate copies from the
saved source directory. Stop the controller and node first, then start them
and check readiness. This maintenance disconnects clients.
.SH CONFIGURATION
hostname, certificate_directory, idp_metadata_file, groups and admin_cidr are
required. Groups are exact case-sensitive IdP names in priority order.
Optional login_hostname defaults to hostname; vpn_network defaults to
10.203.0.0/24; ssh_port to 22; database_name to supivpn.
.PP
The optional database object requires host, ca_file, runtime_password_file and
migration_password_file; port defaults to 5432. Paths must be absolute.
Password inputs must be root-owned regular files, without group/other access
or symlinks, containing distinct single-line printable ASCII passwords.
Use supivpn_runtime and supivpn_migrator logins with the documented grants.
The plan action does not read these files or contact the database.
.PP
Equal subnet pools are allocated to the groups. Internet routing and DNS
remain unchanged. The generated firewall permits only the gateway ping
from VPN clients; review it before applying on a fresh dedicated host.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/supivpn/setup.json
Saved setup inputs; the default configuration for maintenance actions.
.TP
.I /etc/supivpn/controller/database.env
Root-only runtime credentials in systemd EnvironmentFile syntax. Never print
or source as shell code.
.TP
.I /etc/supivpn/controller/migration.env
Separate root-only migration credentials for future explicit upgrades.
.TP
.I /etc/supivpn/firewall.nft
Firewall proposal; never automatically applied.
.SH FAILURE
Partial initialization is preserved for local diagnosis. There is no automatic
rollback, deletion, takeover or credential rotation. Do not remove state on a
working installation to retry initialization.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR supivpn (8),
.BR supivpn-controller (8),
.BR supivpn-migrate (8)
.PP
https://github.com/SupiVPN/supivpn/blob/main/DEPLOYMENT.md
